# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Market split problem {#market-split-problem}"
msgstr "Ang market split problem {#market-split-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The market split problem is a real-world, NP-hard resource allocation problem and has become a benchmark for quantum optimization algorithms.\n"
"It represents a high-stakes logistical challenge: how to partition a complex landscape of customers and products into manageable, equalized territories.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang market split problem ay isang real-world, NP-hard na resource allocation problem at naging benchmark para sa mga quantum optimization algorithm.\n"
"Kumakatawan ito sa isang mataas-ang-taya na logistical na hamon: kung paano hatiin ang isang komplikadong landscape ng mga customer at produkto tungo sa manageable at equalized na mga teritoryo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The goal is to divide $n$ markets into two balanced sales regions such that each region receives exactly half the total demand for $m$ products.\n"
"The solution is the specific configuration that achieves the most even distribution of product demand possible, allowing a company to implement a logistics and staffing strategy where both regions are balanced,\n"
"minimizing the risks such as localized product shortages or warehouse overflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang layunin ay hatiin ang $n$ na markets sa dalawang balanced na sales regions kung saan ang bawat rehiyon ay tumatanggap ng eksaktong kalahati ng total demand para sa $m$ na produkto.\n"
"Ang solusyon ay ang partikular na configuration na nakakamit ng pinaka-even na distribution ng product demand na posible, na nagpapahintulot sa isang kompanya na magpatupad ng logistics at staffing strategy kung saan pantay ang parehong rehiyon,\n"
"na binabawasan ang mga panganib tulad ng localized na product shortages o warehouse overflows.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the number of markets and products increases, the number of possible permutations grows exponentially, making it challenging to find the best split using traditional exhaustive searches.\n"
msgstr "Habang tumataas ang bilang ng markets at produkto, exponentially rin tumataas ang bilang ng posibleng permutations, kaya nahihirapan ang paghahanap ng pinakamahusay na split gamit ang traditional na exhaustive searches.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"
msgstr "Mathematical na formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $A$ be an $m \\times n$ matrix representing the demand of products across markets, where $A_{ij}$ is the demand for product $i$ in market $j$.\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalagay na ang $A$ ay isang $m \\times n$ matrix na kumakatawan sa demand ng mga produkto sa iba't ibang markets, kung saan ang $A_{ij}$ ay ang demand para sa produkto $i$ sa market $j$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A binary assignment vector, $x = [x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n]^T \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$, is defined where:\n"
"* $x_j = 1$ assigns market $j$ to Region A.\n"
"* $x_j = 0$ assigns market $j$ to Region B.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang binary assignment vector, $x = [x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n]^T \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$, ay tinutukoy kung saan:\n"
"* $x_j = 1$ ay itinatalaga ang market $j$ sa Region A.\n"
"* $x_j = 0$ ay itinatalaga ang market $j$ sa Region B.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $d = [d_1, d_2, \\dots, d_m]^T$ be the total demand vector for each product, calculated as $d = A \\cdot \\mathbf{1}$. The target sales volume per region for product $i$ is exactly $\\frac{d_i}{2}$.\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalagay na ang $d = [d_1, d_2, \\dots, d_m]^T$ ay ang total demand vector para sa bawat produkto, kinakalkula bilang $d = A \\cdot \\mathbf{1}$. Ang target sales volume kada rehiyon para sa produkto $i$ ay eksaktong $\\frac{d_i}{2}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization or feasibility constraint requires that the total sales allocated to Region A perfectly matches half the total demand for every product:\n"
msgstr "Ang optimization o feasibility constraint ay hinihiling na ang total sales na inilaan sa Region A ay eksaktong tumutugma sa kalahati ng total demand para sa bawat produkto:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$A x = \\frac{1}{2} A \\mathbf{1} = b.$$\n"
msgstr "$$A x = \\frac{1}{2} A \\mathbf{1} = b.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, because exact division is rarely possible, the problem is formulated to minimize the squared constraint violation (the cost function):\n"
msgstr "Sa praktika, dahil bihirang posible ang eksaktong division, binubuo ang problema para i-minimize ang squared constraint violation (ang cost function):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{x} \\left\\Vert{} A x - b \\right\\Vert{}^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n} A_{ij} x_j - b\\right)^2.$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\min_{x} \\left\\Vert{} A x - b \\right\\Vert{}^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n} A_{ij} x_j - b\\right)^2.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expanding this gives a form that is equivalent to a quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problem.\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinalawak ito, nagbibigay ito ng anyo na katumbas ng quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problem.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upon solving, the solution vector $x$ dictates to which region the market is assigned. This is the configuration that achieves the most balanced distribution of product demand possible.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos malutas, itinatakda ng solution vector $x$ kung saang rehiyon itinalaga ang market. Ito ang configuration na nakakamit ng pinaka-balanced na distribution ng product demand na posible.\n"

